(text "Board includes input AC-coupling capacitors.\nTie A- to ground for this single-ended input.\nUse onboard trim to set volume; start low.\nSD = low shuts amplifier down." (at 276.86 160.02 0) (effects (font (size 1.35 1.35)) (justify left)) (uuid 4fb5769b-68d1-5bbe-b3ec-5414d3a17849))
(text "FIRMWARE ASSUMPTION / CHECK BEFORE BUILD" (at 17.78 200.66 0) (effects (font (size 1.65 1.65)) (justify left)) (uuid 883eceed-d6a1-547d-924e-16d20638cccf))
(text "One AUDIO_PWM GPIO, 3.3 V. Proposed >= 62.5 kHz carrier; vary duty for ~0.5-2 kHz game tones.\nR60/R61 attenuate to at most ~0.30 Vpp before loading. Two RC poles suppress the carrier; values are provisional.\nSilence: steady PWM duty (50% proposed). Check residual carrier, clipping and startup pop on the real board.\nManual mute uses no extra MCU pin; automatic shutdown would need another allocated output." (at 17.78 218.44 0) (effects (font (size 1.35 1.35)) (justify left)) (uuid 8ff52dfe-6f31-5ef3-983f-f7fb9b9bdc1c))
(text "POWER / PORT NOTES" (at 17.78 242.57 0) (effects (font (size 1.55 1.55)) (justify left)) (uuid bbe89035-06b9-5741-8257-3793cf31cd1c))
(text "Use shared 5 V / 3 A load rail, not the ~100 mA PIC supply. Include audio peaks in total load budget.\nC62/C63 near module; short supply/return and twisted speaker pair. Board has additional onboard bypassing.\nU30/LS30 are assembly symbols with logical port labels, not bare-chip or physical header pin numbers.\nSee audio.md for sources and remaining component/volume decisions." (at 17.78 256.54 0) (effects (font (size 1.25 1.25)) (justify left)) (uuid 3b84fcb3-8fb1-5e8a-b189-5cf2d00ca1ac))
(embedded_fonts no))
